== (b) logits vs the pinned dumps — the rule in force is named on every step
  route in force: --gemm library. The cascade floor is ARMED: no step is judged by a cap tighter than the measured hand<->library cascade (cos deficit 2e-03, meanrel 3%), because a route whose dots reassociate cannot be held to a smaller deficit than its own reassociation (bench/route-c-audit-2026-10-14.md §A2), and the per-matmul floor behind it is 1 ULP at every width (A1). Each step line names the floor when it is what made the cap wider.
  where an allowance is priced, the rule is cos deficit <= margin x the step's measured route spread and meanrel <= margin_rel x it, and the margins are THIS FIXTURE's own — read from its own route_allowance.json and derived from its own steps only, so pricing another fixture cannot move them (D-2; the fallback in BAND is 3.50 / 0.42, used only by a file priced before per-fixture keying). Where nothing is priced, the flat published floors apply: cos >= 0.9995 (G5 incremental==batch), meanrel <= 5% (§10.2 cascade ceiling).
  reported: cos vs 0.9999 (G6 decode logits); ndiff and max ULP are reported but not gated (§10.1 F1–F4: a chained dot's legal ndiff is 29–47 %, and a max-ULP bound is blind to a whole-tensor 1-ULP shift)
