== summary
  [note] all 128 of 128 steps judged by the route allowance; the allowance is TIGHTER than the flat §10.1 G5 floor at 110 of them. Worst step 86: deficit = 4.554x its own measured route spread (this fixture's margin in force 7.99, derived as the max ratio inside dec300f alone — engine/route_allowance.py; no other fixture can move it, and no step of this fixture sits outside it by construction).
  [note] 23 of 128 steps sit under G6's decode-logits figure 0.9999 (step:cos — 2:0.999824, 5:0.999899, 24:0.999880, 30:0.999812, 32:0.999899, 39:0.999846, 49:0.999856, 52:0.999897, 60:0.999876, 64:0.999854, 74:0.999871, 85:0.999893 …). G6 is ADVISORY here by decision, not an open question: an end-to-end token carries the whole 24-layer cascade, so it is not judged by a figure belonging to a narrower comparison — see the BAND comment above and the two measured floors in engine/results.md: last-op reassociation 0.99999862 (engine/logits_floor.py) and end-to-end two-legal-routes 1-cos 4.7e-5..1.9e-4 (engine/route_price.py).
  [note] dec300f has a different prompt from dec8, so the overlap check does not apply.
  [note] (g) could NOT prove its own helper on dec300f: this fixture keeps no full per-layer state tensors (`--deep-steps none`), so the fp-of-pins identity has nothing to recompute from, and the conv family cannot be priced at its own extent either. The engine-vs-pin numbers printed for this fixture are still real; what is missing is the proof of the ruler. Run this section on dec64f/dec64t/mt32f, or re-make the fixture with --deep-steps (a re-pin, so a main-agent call: plan §5.1 forbids touching the shipped fixtures).
  [note] (g) could NOT price the conv window on this fixture: the pinned conv buffer is not kept at a step whose newest 3 columns can be pooled (`--deep-steps none`), so inv 2 rests on the engine-side Δ² line above and the extent-mismatched distance, and nothing else. A re-pin with --deep-steps is the only way past that, and re-pinning a shipped fixture is a main-agent call (plan §5.1).
  [note] (g) printed engine-vs-pin state distances and gated none of them. That is the package as planned (§2.6: 'P1 ships a measurement and a tripwire, not a band'); the adopted-threshold decision needs the route spread at the same position, i.e. `engine/route_price.py` extended to state fingerprints, then a `D-x` and a band_history line. Nothing in this run is a band.
  [note] decode_run reported 4.054 ms/step. Timing from a gate run is a by-product, not a measurement: see bench/performance-status.md §6 for what a clean window takes.
  [note] conv window carried across 58 interior wave boundary(ies) at --wave-rows 5, logits inside the cascade band rather than byte-identical to the single-wave run. That is a WEAKER claim than the `--gemm hand` row above, and it has to be read as one: a window read from the wrong rows still moves logits by orders more than the band allows, but the band no longer proves the bytes are the same bytes, because on this route they are not. This is A-04's `T > 1` clause tested, not assumed.
  [note] P4b+P5+P6+P8 launch count on dec300f: the 295-token prompt wave issued 271 batchable launches vs 79945 with --wave-rows 1 (295x fewer); the whole run, 34959 vs 114633, because 128 generation steps are one token wide either way. Counts, never durations — the timing pass is the main agent's (bench/performance-status.md §6) and the command is in engine/results.md.
